=== (A) on-shell 2->2 umklapp fraction vs incoming energy, folded fine lattice d = 2 ===
N= 4 (E_max=  11.4): umklapp fraction in E_in/E_max bins of 0.2:    -      -   0.000  0.000  0.073  0.263  0.475  0.533  0.493  0.456 
N= 8 (E_max=  22.6): umklapp fraction in E_in/E_max bins of 0.2:    -   0.000  0.000  0.005  0.086  0.265  0.478  0.534  0.530  0.414 
N=16 (E_max=  45.3): umklapp fraction in E_in/E_max bins of 0.2:    -      -   0.000  0.003  0.100  0.254  0.491  0.534  0.527  0.444 
-> the curves coincide in E/E_max (E_max ~ 2 sqrt(2) N): tower umklapp switches on at a fixed fraction of the
   truncation-edge energy and is O(1) above it, for every N.

   thermal umklapp fraction Gamma_U/Gamma (Boltzmann incoming pairs, same on-shell weights), T in coarse units
N= 4: T=   2: 2.30e-01  T=   4: 3.76e-01  T=   8: 4.28e-01  T=  16: 4.48e-01  T=  32: 4.56e-01
N= 8: T=   2: 2.98e-02  T=   4: 2.31e-01  T=   8: 3.75e-01  T=  16: 4.27e-01  T=  32: 4.46e-01
N=16: T=   2: 7.72e-06  T=   4: 1.92e-02  T=   8: 2.18e-01  T=  16: 3.69e-01  T=  32: 4.24e-01
-> at fixed T the umklapp fraction falls like exp(-E_th/T) with E_th proportional to N; at T ~ N it is O(1).

