d=2 N= 64: flat fraction 0.5542   basketball-weighted fraction 0.3630
d=3 N=  4: flat fraction 0.7047   basketball-weighted fraction 0.6213
d=3 N= 16: flat fraction 0.7054   basketball-weighted fraction 0.6179
d=3 N= 64: flat fraction 0.7032   basketball-weighted fraction 0.6149
   exact flat values: d=1: 1/3, d=2: 5/9, d=3: 19/27 = 0.7037 (sum of three uniforms leaves the zone)
-> N-independent: in loops, most of the contact-vertex phase space is tower umklapp, for every N.

=== (C) N-band cells without an internal Z_N label: low-band tower umklapp from a cell-site contact vertex ===
  process: bands (0,0) -> (1,0) at coarse momenta k1 + k2 = k3 + k4 (tower mismatch 2 pi: a LOW-energy tower umklapp)
  ratio = |V_umklapp| / |V_normal (0,0)->(0,0)|, vertex V = sum_j psi1 psi2 conj(psi3 psi4) over cell sites
N= 4: delta=0e+00: 2.93e-16  delta=1e-03: 8.59e-04  delta=1e-02: 7.52e-03  delta=1e-01: 1.07e-01
N= 8: delta=0e+00: 9.71e-16  delta=1e-03: 1.53e-03  delta=1e-02: 3.59e-02  delta=1e-01: 1.57e-01
N=16: delta=0e+00: 5.29e-15  delta=1e-03: 5.17e-03  delta=1e-02: 6.33e-02  delta=1e-01: 2.97e-01
-> with the exact Z_N (fine translation) the low-band tower umklapp vertex vanishes (machine zero); any breaking
   of it switches on tower umklapp among the LOWEST bands, linearly in the breaking.  Tower-normal contact
   interactions among N bands require the internal Z_N label, i.e. the network to be a fine lattice of spacing a/N.
